{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'name-environment|:status :ok' test/yin/vm/linker/authority_test.cljc | head -35; sed -n '235,265p' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc; sed -n '1350,1378p' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc; sed -n '1,60p' bb.edn\"","aggregated_output":"rg: test/yin/vm/linker/authority_test.cljc: IO error for operation on test/yin/vm/linker/authority_test.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n                           (map (fn [cand]\n                                  {:address (get (:env cand)\n                                                 :yin.module/manifest)\n                                   :asserter (:principal cand)})\n                                cands)))\n        addresses (distinct (map :address entries))\n        asserters (distinct (map :asserter entries))]\n    (case (count addresses)\n      0 {:status :refused :reason :absent}\n      1 {:status :ok\n         :address (first addresses)\n         :yin.link/provenance\n         {:yin.module/asserted-by (vec asserters)\n          :yin.link/proof-kind\n          (vec (distinct (map (fn [p] (get (get decls p) :proof))\n                              asserters)))\n          :yin.link/snapshot snapshot}}\n      {:status :refused\n       :reason :ambiguous-name\n       :addresses (vec addresses)\n       :asserters (vec asserters)})))\n\n\n(defn name-environment\n  \"Fold `events` under `authority` into the name-environment snapshot\n   of section 8.2.\n\n   `authority` is a map with the snapshot under :snapshot (an index\n   manifest address or a stream cursor; it is echoed and never\n   dereferenced here) and the accepted principals under :principals.\n   A signature principal declares {:proof :yin.module/signature\n                                 slots\n                                 (drop 2 row)))))]\n    (or (when (reserved-var? root)\n          (merge (defect-res :reserved-name root)\n                 {:role :variable, :name definition-operator}))\n        (some own rows)\n        (when-let [[id suffix] (some misplaced rows)]\n          (merge (defect-res :reserved-name id suffix)\n                 {:role :variable, :name definition-operator})))))\n\n\n(defn validate-rows\n  \"§7.4: validate a projected row set before reconstruction. `rows` is\n   `{id [id tag & slots]}`; `root` is the root row's id.\n\n   Returns nil when every row is well-formed, else the first defect as\n   `{:rule r :path p}`, or `{:rule :root-reachable :id id}` for a row of the\n   loaded set nothing reaches. Rules run in §7.4's order -- `:tag`,\n   `:arity`, `:slot-kind`, `:saturation`, `:id-resolves`, `:acyclic`,\n   `:root-reachable`, then Rule R's `:reserved-name` -- discovered by\n   descending from the root row, so a path is always available except for\n   `:root-reachable`'s unreached rows. Each rule assumes the earlier ones\n   held.\"\n  [{:keys [root rows]}]\n  (let [safe-tag (fn [row] (when (and (vector? row) (<= 2 (count row))) (nth row 1)))\n        safe-slots (fn [tag] (get semantic-bytecode-grammar tag))\n        safe-children (fn [id]\n                        (let [row (get rows id)]\n                          (if row\n{:tasks\n {test:clj {:doc \"Run JVM tests (via clj); the DHT process test needs the Node REPL build\"\n            :depends [build:yin-repl-node]\n            :task (shell \"clojure -M:test\")}\n\n  build:yin-repl-node\n  {:doc \"Compile the Node yin.repl (shadow-cljs build :yin-repl) to target/yin-repl.js\"\n   ;; yin.repl.dht-process-test spawns it as the JVM-to-Node reader of\n   ;; DHT epic S5, a required leg: a missing build fails that test.\n   :task (shell \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile yin-repl\")}\n\n  test:cljs {:doc \"Run Node tests (via shadow-cljs with :cljs alias)\"\n             :task (shell \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test\")}\n\n  build:yin-repl-peer\n  {:doc \"Compile the yin.repl R5 cross-host peer (client role and --serve server role) as a Dart exe\"\n   ;; Process B of the R5 slice is a whole program rather than a test\n   ;; namespace, and this project's cljd.core carries the Flutter extensions,\n   ;; so only an ahead-of-time build is a peer the plain Dart VM can start.\n   ;; It is compiled alone and first: the test build rewrites the same\n   ;; cljd-out tree, so a peer built after it would import a tree it does\n   ;; not match.  The R5 cross-host tests spawn this one exe from the JVM\n   ;; and Node lanes, so `bb test` builds it first; a bare `bb test:clj` or\n   ;; `bb test:cljs` without it skips those tests with a printed notice\n   ;; rather than failing.\n   :task (do (shell \"mkdir -p build\")\n             (shell \"clojure -M:cljd compile yin.repl.slice-peer\")\n             (shell \"dart compile exe lib/cljd-out/yin/repl/slice-peer.dart -o build/yin-repl-peer\"))}\n\n  test:cljd {:doc \"Run Dart tests (via clojure -M:cljd)\"\n             :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\n             :task (shell \"clojure -M:cljd test\")}\n\n  test {:doc \"Run all tests (cross-host R5 pairs need the Dart peer, and the DHT process test the Node REPL, so build them first)\"\n        :depends [build:yin-repl-peer build:yin-repl-node test:clj test:cljs test:cljd]}}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
